# What must never leave this machine.
#
# This repository is public, so anything committed here is published to
# everyone who browses it, and to everyone who clones it to run their own
# instance.
#
# THREAT_MODEL.md spends its length arguing that a breach of the public box
# should yield only the already-published record. A `git add .` without this
# file hands over more than a breach of the box ever could, because the box
# runs in public_mirror mode and this directory does not.
#
# Rule: this file denies whole DIRECTORIES, not extensions. A rule like
# "*.token" protects the files you thought of; "data/" protects the ones you
# did not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE OPERATIONAL DATA. 313 MB, 22,849 files.
#
#   data/sparrow.db     2,348 sightings, and the node table holds TRUE lat/lon.
#                       Publishing it defeats the 44 m jitter that exists to
#                       keep a volunteer's home address out of the record -
#                       for every node, including the ones that are not his.
#   data/snaps/         2,716 photographs of vehicles on a real street.
#   data/training/      19,790 crops, private-tier included.
#   data/operator.token the credential that can retract, promote and CONFIRM,
#                       and confirming is what makes a plate searchable.
#   data/models/        the trained head - his labels, not redistributable
#                       without deciding to.
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAMERA CREDENTIALS AND TRUE POSITION.
#
# placement.json carries node_id AND token together. The token is a BEARER
# credential: whoever holds it owns that camera - can post as it, move it,
# rename it. It also carries the camera's true lat/lon, unjittered.
camctl/placement.json

# TLS private key for the LAN https listener the phone nodes use.
certs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL STATE, not settings anyone else should inherit.
#
# config.json is the LAN hub's config: operator auth OFF, public_mirror OFF.
# Publishing it would invite someone to launch a public box carrying the
# development posture. config.launch.json is the one to copy, and it IS
# committed, with the reason for each value written beside it.
config.json
logs/
*.log
*.err

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD AND ENVIRONMENT
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE OPERATOR'S MACHINE, not the project.
#
# These are launchers and one-shot scripts wired to a specific PC: absolute
# D: paths, a venv location, a hostname, and registration into a private
# cockpit and pages hub that only exist on that machine. They would not run
# for anybody else, and publishing them advertises the layout and the machine
# name of the person running the cameras for no benefit to a reader.
Resume Sparrow.ps1
Start Sparrow.bat
Start Camera Node.bat
camctl/Start Camera Control.bat
register.py
register_camctl.py
vmlab/

# The brand GENERATORS read a source photo from a personal folder. The
# finished marks (png/ico) are kept - they are what a contributor needs.
brand/*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LARGE FIXTURES AND WEIGHTS the public box never loads.
#
# testvideo/ is 94 MB of Wikimedia sample clips used for offline detector
# runs. The mirror does not detect anything, so it is dead weight in a clone.
#
# The .pt weights are Ultralytics (AGPL) and are detector-side only - the
# mirror imports neither cv2 nor ultralytics. Left out deliberately rather
# than by accident: a node operator downloads them, a mirror never needs them.
#
# NOTE public/vendor/ is NOT ignored, on purpose. The browser detector loads
# ort-wasm-simd-threaded.wasm and yolo11s.onnx (36 MB) directly from this
# server, and no CDN can reach a LAN phone. Those two files are the
# contributor app working or not working.
testvideo/
*.pt
.wrangler/

# Pre-edit snapshots. Harmless individually, but an untracked file that never
# goes away leaves `git status` permanently dirty - and a dirty status is a
# status nobody reads, which is how the box drifted for days without anyone
# noticing. The live file is committed; the snapshot's content is in git
# history if it is ever wanted.
*.bak

# 🔐 A camera's PRIVATE signing key. Never leaves the machine that owns the
# camera, so it must never reach the repo either - and the public half is the
# only part the hub is ever sent.
keys/

# 🚨 PyInstaller output. NEVER COMMIT THESE. The build tree contains absolute
# paths from the machine that built it (preflight caught exactly that: home
# paths inside xref-SparrowMap.html), and the exe itself is tens of megabytes
# of derived artefact. The app is built from desktop/build.py on demand.
desktop/build/
desktop/dist/
desktop/*.spec

# The CPU-only virtualenv used to build the desktop app. Third-party
# site-packages, not this project's code.
desktop/.buildenv/
tools/measure_public_cams.py
public/snapshot.json
camsurvey/

# 🚨 GENERATED ON THE SERVER, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS IGNORED.
# tools/support_page.py builds this from the LIVE database and from the machine's
# own memory and disk, so it can only be produced on the box. Committing it would
# mean either a stale copy overwriting the real one on every deploy, or the box
# showing as drifted from origin/main forever - deploy.py verifies that tree
# match and it should keep failing loudly for real drift.
# (public/checksums.html is DIFFERENT: it is built from published release assets,
# so it is reproducible anywhere and is tracked.)
public/support.html

# Personal-data working drafts (abuse reports, email/reply drafts). They hold
# real addresses and IPs, so they stay local and never reach this public repo -
# preflight's personal-data gate fails on them by design if they ever get added.
docs/abuse_reports_*.md
docs/email_replies_*.md
docs/replies_*.md

# Local RavenMap DevTest runtime state
devtest/
camctl/proof.html

tools/.sparrow_claude_state.json
tools/.sparrow_claude_state.json.lock
tools/claude_poll.err
tools/inbox_media/
scratch/
# Downloaded IEEE OUI registry (~240k lines) used by the local RF scanner;
# regenerable data, and the map box does not run the scanner - keep it out of git.
rf/oui.txt
tools/.claude_mesh_rat.json
tools/.claude_mesh_rat.json.lock
